### Procedure templates — smoke test for immutable versions and stable keys.
#
# Run top to bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP client (or VS Code REST Client with
# the same syntax). Each request stores what the next one needs.
#
# Prerequisites: docker compose up -d, .\setup-keycloak.ps1, .\setup-openfga.ps1,
# .\setup-demo-users.ps1 (seeds the properties used at the end), and the
# procedure service running on :8095.
#
# @host targets the service directly. Through the gateway use
# http://localhost:8080 once its procedure-service route includes
# /api/v1/procedure-templates/** (a bearer token needs no session or CSRF).

@host = http://localhost:8095
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180

### Token for testuser (org 1111…1111, OpenFGA admin)
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/sclera/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=sclera-app&username=testuser&password=testuser

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 1. Create a template — also creates draft v1. Keys are minted: s1, q2, o3, o4
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fire safety walk {{$random.integer(1000, 9999)}}",
  "description": "Daily walk-through",
  "definition": {
    "items": [
      { "text": "Fire exits", "type": "SECTION" },
      { "text": "Is the fire exit clear?", "type": "YES_NO", "required": true,
        "workOrder": true, "alertProfile": "ap-fire", "standard": "NFPA 10",
        "options": [
          { "label": "Yes", "result": "PASS" },
          { "label": "No",  "result": "FAIL" }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

> {% client.global.set("id", response.body.data.id); %}

### 2. Read the draft — note the keys and rowVersion
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

> {% client.global.set("rowVersion", response.body.data.rowVersion); %}

### 3. Save the draft — send keys back for existing items, omit for new ones (the follow-up gets one)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rowVersion": {{rowVersion}},
  "changeNote": "Reworded q2, added a photo",
  "definition": {
    "items": [
      { "key": "s1", "text": "Fire exits", "type": "SECTION" },
      { "key": "q2", "text": "Is every fire exit clear?", "type": "YES_NO", "required": true,
        "workOrder": true, "alertProfile": "ap-fire", "standard": "NFPA 10",
        "options": [
          { "key": "o3", "label": "Yes", "result": "PASS" },
          { "key": "o4", "label": "No",  "result": "FAIL" }
        ],
        "follow": [
          { "text": "Describe the obstruction", "type": "TEXT", "required": true, "when": "o4" }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

> {% client.global.set("rowVersion", response.body.data.rowVersion); %}

### 4. Save with a stale rowVersion — expect 409
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rowVersion": 0, "definition": { "items": [] } }

### 5. Publish — creates v1 (PUBLISHED, frozen)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rowVersion": {{rowVersion}} }

### 6. Start a new draft from v1 — this is how you edit after publishing (v2)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromVersionNo": 1 }

### 7. Publish it unchanged — expect newVersion=false, returns v1, draft discarded
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Draft again, then add a second section and a number question
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromVersionNo": 1 }

> {% client.global.set("rowVersion", response.body.data.rowVersion); %}

###
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rowVersion": {{rowVersion}},
  "changeNote": "Split out extinguishers",
  "definition": {
    "items": [
      { "key": "s1", "text": "Fire exits", "type": "SECTION" },
      { "key": "q2", "text": "Is every fire exit clear?", "type": "YES_NO", "required": true,
        "workOrder": true, "alertProfile": "ap-fire", "standard": "NFPA 10",
        "options": [
          { "key": "o3", "label": "Yes", "result": "PASS" },
          { "key": "o4", "label": "No",  "result": "FAIL" }
        ],
        "follow": [
          { "key": "q5", "text": "Describe the obstruction", "type": "TEXT", "required": true, "when": "o4" }
        ]
      },
      { "text": "Extinguishers", "type": "SECTION" },
      { "text": "Record the gauge reading", "type": "INTEGER", "unit": "psi", "min": 100, "max": 175 }
    ]
  }
}

### 9. Publish — creates v2
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Version history — v2, v1
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/versions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. One version with its full document
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/versions/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Diff v1 → v2 — a section and a question added
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/diff?from=1&to=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Template summary — currentPublishedVersionNo and draftVersionNo
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. List
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates?status=ACTIVE&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Rename (identity only — not versioned)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Fire safety walk (renamed) {{$random.integer(1000, 9999)}}", "description": "Weekly walk-through" }

### 16. Clone v2 into a new template (draft v1, same keys)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/clone
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Fire safety walk copy {{$random.integer(1000, 9999)}}", "fromVersionNo": 2 }

### 17. Archive — versions stay readable, no more drafts
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 18. Tenant isolation — as testuser2 (org 2222…2222) the template is not visible
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/sclera/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=sclera-app&username=testuser2&password=testuser2

> {% client.global.set("token2", response.body.access_token); %}

### expect 403 — testuser2 has no relation to this template in OpenFGA
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token2}}

###############################################################################
# Property isolation (VDMS)
#
# X-Sclera-Property says which property you are looking at. Omit it and you are
# at organization level, seeing only procedures shared across the organization;
# send it and you see that property's plus the shared ones. Another property's
# are not filtered out of the answer — they never enter it.
#
# Run .\setup-demo-users.ps1 first; it seeds these two and prints them.
###############################################################################

@vdms001 = aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@vdms002 = aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000002

### demo-admin — reaches every property in the org, without a per-property grant
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/sclera/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=sclera-app&username=demo-admin&password=demo-admin

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### demo-inspector — granted VDMS001 only
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/sclera/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=sclera-app&username=demo-inspector&password=demo-inspector

> {% client.global.set("inspectorToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### P1. Author a procedure inside VDMS001 — it belongs to VDMS001
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Sclera-Property: {{vdms001}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Extinguisher check — VDMS001", "definition": { "items": [
  { "text": "Is it in place?", "type": "YES_NO", "required": true,
    "options": [ { "label": "Yes", "result": "PASS" }, { "label": "No", "result": "FAIL" } ] } ] } }

### P2. Author one inside VDMS002
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Sclera-Property: {{vdms002}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Boiler check — VDMS002", "definition": { "items": [
  { "text": "Pressure in range?", "type": "YES_NO",
    "options": [ { "label": "Yes", "result": "PASS" }, { "label": "No", "result": "FAIL" } ] } ] } }

### P3. Author one at organization level — no header, so shared by every property
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Site induction — shared", "definition": { "items": [
  { "text": "Briefing given?", "type": "YES_NO",
    "options": [ { "label": "Yes", "result": "PASS" }, { "label": "No", "result": "FAIL" } ] } ] } }

### P4. Inside VDMS001 — expect the VDMS001 one and the shared one, not VDMS002's
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Sclera-Property: {{vdms001}}

### P5. Inside VDMS002 — expect the VDMS002 one and the shared one, not VDMS001's
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Sclera-Property: {{vdms002}}

### P6. Organization level — expect only the shared one
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### P7. demo-inspector inside VDMS001 — allowed, same view as the admin has here
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{inspectorToken}}
X-Sclera-Property: {{vdms001}}

### P8. demo-inspector asking for VDMS002 — expect 403, refused before the database
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{inspectorToken}}
X-Sclera-Property: {{vdms002}}

### P9. A malformed property — expect 400
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procedure-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Sclera-Property: not-a-uuid

### M1. Which properties may demo-admin open? — expect VDMS001 and VDMS002
# What the property switcher lists. Read from the grants, so it never offers a
# property the X-Sclera-Property check would then refuse.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/me/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### M2. Which properties may demo-inspector open? — expect VDMS001 only
GET {{host}}/api/v1/me/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{inspectorToken}}
